IMPORT prelude

-- Immigration Act 1959 (Singapore) -- entering, leaving and staying: ss 5 to 9AA (entry and departure, prohibited
-- immigrants, entry bans, no-boarding directives), ss 10 to 15 (entry and re-entry permits, loss of citizenship,
-- cancellation, overstaying), s 36 (return after removal) and ss 39A and 39B (no judicial review, no hearing).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ (amendments
-- to Act 31 of 2023, Act 5 of 2025 and Act 16 of 2026).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 48 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository, mostly for s 2 definitions (25)
-- and s 3 (10). SCOPED. Not encoded: visas (Part 2A), arrival procedure and carriers' passenger information (Part 4),
-- removal and detention (Part 5), information sharing (Part 5A), cross-border railway pre-clearance (Part 5B), and the
-- enforcement powers in Part 6.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Immigration Act 1959 -- entry and status`

§§ `5 -- entering and leaving only at authorised places`

-- s 5(2), (4): a person must not, "unless compelled by accident or other reasonable cause", enter or leave Singapore
-- except at an authorised place. (5): an offence -- no penalty stated, so the s 58 general penalty: $2,000 or 6 months.
-- This binds citizens too.
GIVEN `at an authorised place` IS A BOOLEAN, `compelled by accident or other reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the crossing is an offence under section 5` IF
    (NOT `at an authorised place`) AND (NOT `compelled by accident or other reasonable cause`)

§§ `6, 7 -- who may enter`

-- s 7(1): "A citizen of Singapore is entitled to enter Singapore without having obtained a permit or pass". (2): "The
-- burden of proof that any person is a citizen of Singapore shall lie upon that person."
-- s 6(1): a non-citizen must not enter unless (a) holding a valid entry or re-entry permit, (b) named on one and
-- accompanying the holder, (c) holding a valid pass, or (d) exempted.
-- s 6(3)(a): "imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months and SHALL ALSO be punished with caning with not less than
-- 3 strokes" (or a fine of up to $6,000 in lieu where the person cannot be caned).
DECLARE Entrant HAS
    `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a valid entry or re-entry permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is endorsed on a permit and with its holder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a valid pass` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is exempted by order` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the entrant` IS AN Entrant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may lawfully enter` IF
        `the entrant`'s `is a citizen`
    OR  `the entrant`'s `holds a valid entry or re-entry permit`
    OR  `the entrant`'s `is endorsed on a permit and with its holder`
    OR  `the entrant`'s `holds a valid pass`
    OR  `the entrant`'s `is exempted by order`

GIVEN `the entrant` IS AN Entrant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `caning is mandatory for the unlawful entry` IF
    NOT `the person may lawfully enter` `the entrant`

§§ `8 -- prohibited immigrants`

-- s 8(1): a non-citizen who is a member of a prohibited class, "or who, in the opinion of the Controller, is a member",
-- is a prohibited immigrant. (4): "The burden of proof that any person seeking to enter Singapore is not a prohibited
-- immigrant shall lie upon that person."
-- s 8(3) lists the classes. Among them:
--   (a) unable to show means of support or definite employment, or likely to become a charge on the public;
--   (ba) "any person suffering from Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome or infected with the Human Immunodeficiency
--        Virus";
--   (d) convicted in ANY country of an offence for which ANY term of imprisonment was passed, not pardoned, and deemed
--       undesirable by the Controller;
--   (e) a prostitute, or a person who lived on or received the proceeds of prostitution;
--   (g) vagrants or habitual beggars;
--   (i) a person who "disbelieves in or is opposed to established government";
--   (n) "the family and dependants of a prohibited immigrant".
-- s 8(2)(b): a prohibited immigrant (other than one banned under s 9) may enter only with a pass issuable to prohibited
-- immigrants under the regulations.
--
-- (ba) is unqualified: HIV infection alone makes a non-citizen a prohibited immigrant. (n) makes prohibition hereditary:
-- the family of a prohibited immigrant are prohibited themselves, with no class of their own required. (i) reaches
-- belief alone -- "disbelieves in" established government.
DECLARE ProhibitedClass IS ONE OF
    `cannot show means of support`
    `a dangerous contagious disease`
    `AIDS or HIV infection`
    `refused a medical examination`
    `an imprisonment sentence anywhere, unpardoned, and deemed undesirable`
    `a prostitute or living on prostitution`
    `procuring prostitutes`
    `a vagrant or habitual beggar`
    `entry was unlawful`
    `opposed to or disbelieving in established government`
    `in a subversive organisation`
    `deemed undesirable by the Minister on information received`
    `removed elsewhere and deemed undesirable`
    `lacking valid travel documents`
    `family or dependant of a prohibited immigrant`
    `banned by an order under section 9`
    `none`

GIVEN `the class` IS A ProhibitedClass, `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a prohibited immigrant` IF
        NOT `is a citizen`
    AND CONSIDER `the class`
        WHEN `none` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- A conviction in any country counts only with an imprisonment sentence, no free pardon, and the Controller's view.
DECLARE ForeignConviction HAS
    `a sentence of imprisonment was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Controller deems the person undesirable` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conviction` IS A ForeignConviction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conviction puts the person in class (d)` IF
        `the conviction`'s `a sentence of imprisonment was passed`
    AND NOT `the conviction`'s `received a free pardon`
    AND `the conviction`'s `the Controller deems the person undesirable`

DECLARE ProhibitedEntry HAS
    `banned by a section 9 order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a pass issuable to prohibited immigrants` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempted under section 56` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the entry` IS A ProhibitedEntry
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prohibited immigrant may enter` IF
        `the entry`'s `exempted under section 56`
    OR  (    NOT `the entry`'s `banned by a section 9 order`
         AND `the entry`'s `holds a pass issuable to prohibited immigrants`)

§§ `9 -- entry bans`

-- s 9(1)(a): the Minister may prohibit or limit entry "in the interests of public security or public health, or by
-- reason of any economic, industrial, social, educational or other conditions". (1A): an order other than one for
-- public security or public health does not apply to a person OUTSIDE Singapore holding a valid re-entry permit or pass.
-- (2): no order applies to a citizen. (3): a class order (other than security or health) must go to Parliament and may
-- be annulled within 3 months. (5): breach -- "a presumptive minimum term of not less than 2 years and not more than
-- 4 years" and a fine up to $6,000.
DECLARE BanFacts HAS
    `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the order is for public security or public health` IS A BOOLEAN
    `outside Singapore when the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a valid re-entry permit or pass` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A BanFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ban applies to the person` IF
        NOT `the facts`'s `is a citizen`
    AND (    `the facts`'s `the order is for public security or public health`
         OR  NOT (`the facts`'s `outside Singapore when the order was made` AND `the facts`'s `holds a valid re-entry permit or pass`))

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the presumptive minimum years for breaching a ban` MEANS 2

§§ `9AA -- no-boarding directives`

-- s 9AA(2): a directive must not issue "(a) against a citizen ...; (b) on the ground [the person's presence would be
-- undesirable] against a person who holds a valid permit or pass; or (c) on the ground [the person would not be issued
-- a permit or pass] against a person who intends to board ... for the purpose of transiting". (6): the Controller "is
-- not required to serve the no-boarding directive on the subject person, or otherwise inform" them. (7)(a), (8): each
-- carrier notified is liable to $10,000 if the person arrives -- a STRICT LIABILITY offence.
DECLARE NoBoardGround IS ONE OF
    `a prohibited immigrant`
    `covered by an entry ban`
    `a risk to safety or health`
    `presence would be undesirable`
    `would not be issued a permit or pass`

DECLARE NoBoardFacts HAS
    `the ground` IS A NoBoardGround
    `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a valid permit or pass` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is transiting` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A NoBoardFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a no-boarding directive may issue` IF
        NOT `the facts`'s `is a citizen`
    AND CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the ground`
        WHEN `presence would be undesirable` THEN NOT `the facts`'s `holds a valid permit or pass`
        WHEN `would not be issued a permit or pass` THEN NOT `the facts`'s `is transiting`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person must be told of the directive` IF
    FALSE

§§ `11, 14A -- permanent residents abroad`

-- s 11(1A): a permanent resident "who is outside Singapore without a valid re-entry permit must apply for a re-entry
-- permit within the prescribed period" (the period is in regulations, not retrieved). (1C): the duty continues even if
-- they re-enter on a pass. s 14A(1): the entry permit -- permanent residence -- is CANCELLED AUTOMATICALLY if they do not
-- apply in time, or if the application is rejected. s 11(2A): the Controller may refuse a re-entry permit.
DECLARE PRAbroad HAS
    `outside Singapore without a valid re-entry permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applied within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applied before the period began and it was pending or later rejected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application was rejected` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the pr` IS A PRAbroad
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permanent residence is cancelled automatically` IF
        `the pr`'s `outside Singapore without a valid re-entry permit`
    AND (    (    NOT `the pr`'s `applied within the prescribed period`
              AND NOT `the pr`'s `applied before the period began and it was pending or later rejected`)
         OR  `the pr`'s `the application was rejected`)

§§ `11A -- losing citizenship while in Singapore`

-- s 11A(1): a person in Singapore who ceases to be a citizen "must not remain in Singapore for more than 24 HOURS"
-- without a permit or pass, unless they apply within that time (then they may stay pending the decision, and must leave
-- within 24 hours of a rejection). (6): the overstay penalties below.
GIVEN `hours since ceasing to be a citizen` IS A NUMBER, `applied within 24 hours` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a permit or pass` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the former citizen is unlawfully in Singapore` IF
        `hours since ceasing to be a citizen` GREATER THAN 24
    AND NOT `applied within 24 hours`
    AND NOT `holds a permit or pass`

§§ `12 -- endorsing a wife and children`

-- s 12: the Controller may, on application by the holder, "endorse upon the permit, pass or certificate ... the name or
-- names of the WIFE or child of that person."
--
-- The text provides for a wife, not a husband or spouse. A female permit-holder has no route under s 12 to endorse her
-- husband, and s 6(1)(b) lets only an ENDORSED person enter on another's permit.
DECLARE Relative IS ONE OF
    `wife`
    `husband`
    `child`
    `parent`

GIVEN `the relative` IS A Relative
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the relative may be endorsed on the holder's permit` IF
    CONSIDER `the relative`
    WHEN `wife` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `child` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `14, 15 -- cancellation and overstaying`

-- s 14(3): if the holder is a prohibited immigrant, the Controller MUST cancel. s 14(4): if a material statement was
-- false, the holder is a prohibited immigrant, or the holder contravened the Act, the regulations or a condition, the
-- Controller MAY cancel "and may declare AT ANY TIME after the date of the entry ... that the presence of that person in
-- Singapore is unlawful." (5): cancelling a re-entry permit for breach of ITS condition lets the Controller cancel the
-- ENTRY permit too, "whether or not that person has contravened any condition of the entry permit".
-- s 15(3): remaining after cancellation or expiry, without reasonable cause --
--   (a) up to 90 days: $4,000 or 6 months or both;
--   (b) over 90 days: "SHALL ... be punished with imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months and SHALL ALSO be
--       punished with caning with not less than 3 strokes".
--
-- Day 90 and day 91 fall on opposite sides of a line between a fine and mandatory imprisonment with caning.
GIVEN `days overstayed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment and caning are mandatory for the overstay` IF
    `days overstayed` GREATER THAN 90

GIVEN `days overstayed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the overstay may be punished by a fine alone` IF
        `days overstayed` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `days overstayed` AT MOST 90

DECLARE CancellationGround IS ONE OF
    `the holder is a prohibited immigrant`
    `a false material statement`
    `breach of the Act, regulations or a condition`
    `the holder's political views`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A CancellationGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Controller must cancel` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `the holder is a prohibited immigrant` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A CancellationGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Controller may cancel` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `the holder's political views` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- (The "political views" fixture is no answer in practice: s 8(3)(i) makes a person "opposed to established government"
-- a prohibited immigrant, and so within the first ground.)

§§ `36 -- coming back after removal`

-- s 36(1): a person removed must not enter or reside without the Controller's prior written permission. (2): "a
-- presumptive minimum term of not less than one year and not more than 3 years" and up to $6,000.
GIVEN `was removed` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Controller's prior written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the return is an offence` IF
    `was removed` AND NOT `has the Controller's prior written permission`

§§ `39A, 39B -- no judicial review, no hearing`

-- s 39A(1): "There shall be no judicial review in any court of any act done or decision made by the Minister or the
-- Controller under any provision of this Act EXCEPT in regard to any question relating to compliance with any
-- PROCEDURAL requirement". (2): includes quashing, mandatory and prohibiting orders, declarations, injunctions, an Order
-- for Review of Detention (habeas corpus), and "any other suit or action".
-- s 39B: the Controller or Minister "is not required to give any person ... an opportunity to be heard".
--
-- Read together: the only reviewable ground is procedural non-compliance, and s 39B removes the procedural requirement
-- most often relied on.
DECLARE ReviewGround IS ONE OF
    `breach of a procedural requirement in the Act or regulations`
    `no opportunity to be heard`
    `irrationality`
    `error of law`
    `unlawful detention`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A ReviewGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a court may review the decision on the ground` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `breach of a procedural requirement in the Act or regulations` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
